    "afterSuccess": {
      "data": "Lifting each step (Clean Each, then Chart Each) and using the pre-lifted whole (Process Each) both produced the same batch of charts. That's functoriality: F(g∘f) = F(g)∘F(f) — lifting a composite equals composing the lifts.",
      "alchemy": "Lifting each step and using the pre-lifted whole both produced the same crate. F(g∘f) = F(g)∘F(f).",
      "spellcraft": "Lifting each step and using the pre-lifted whole both produced the same flock. F(g∘f) = F(g)∘F(f).",
      "abstract": "Both routes produced the same F(C): F(g∘f) = F(g)∘F(f)."
    },
    "summary": "Functors preserve composition: lifting a whole pipeline equals lifting each step and composing — F(g ∘ f) = F(g) ∘ F(f).",
    "notation": ["F(g ∘ f) = F(g) ∘ F(f)"],
    "moreFormal": "With identity preservation, this is the full definition of a functor: it carries every commuting diagram in C to a commuting diagram in D.",
    "programmerAnalogy": "map(compose(g, f)) === compose(map(g), map(f))."
  },
